Throwaway test vector. The key protects nothing.

master.key and greeting.enc were written by the v0.1.0 data plane
(git show v0.1.0:core/kernel/data_plane/__init__.py). master.key is the
44-byte Fernet key that release creates. greeting.enc is
store_encrypted("greeting", ...) under that key.

tests/test_keys.py checks that the data plane opens this deployment through
every key provider. Do not regenerate these files: their value is that the
v0.1.0 code made them.

agents/ was written by the v0.1.0 agent runtime
(git show v0.1.0:core/kernel/agent_runtime/__init__.py): an agent registered
with memory, then saved, a message published on "orders", then a task created.
v0.1.0 cannot serialize a task (TaskPriority is not JSON serializable), so
tasks/tasks.json is the truncated file it writes: what a v0.1.0 deployment
that created a task has on disk. tests/test_state_encryption.py loads this
directory with agent state encryption on.
